    "preview": "[1811.12799] Customer Lifetime Value in Video Games Using Deep Learning and Parametric Models\nSkip to main content\nSearch\nSubmit\nDonate\nLog in\nSearch arXiv\nPress Enter to search ·\nAdvanced search\nComputer Science > Computers and Society\narXiv:1811.12799\n(cs)\n[Submitted on 28 Nov 2018]\nTitle:\nCustomer Lifetime Value in Video Games Using Deep Learning and Parametric Models\nAuthors:\nPei Pei Chen\n,\nAnna Guitart\n,\nAna Fernández del Río\n,\nÁfrica Periáñez\nView a PDF of the paper titled Customer Lifetime Value in Video Games Using Deep Learning and Parametric Models, by Pei Pei Chen and 2 other authors\nView PDF\nHTML (experimental)\nAbstract:\nNowadays, video game developers record every virtual action performed by their players. As each player can remain in the game for years, this results in an exceptionally rich dataset that can be used to understand and predict player behavior. In particular, this information may serve to identify the most valuable players and foresee the amount of money they"
